problem_statement:
Range requests do not work for files larger 2GB
**Actual behavior (the bug)**
When offering a large file via Context.seekableStream the maximum size is incorrectly reported and requests for data beyond the first 2GB cause IndexOutOfBounds exceptions.

**Expected behavior**
Files > 2GB can be correctly downloaded via range requests.

**To Reproduce**
```
app.get("/file", ctx -> {
    File file = new File("/large-file.bin"); //must be > 2GB in size
    ctx.seekableStream(new FileInputStream(file), "application/octet-stream");
});
// curl http://localhost:7000/file --head
// curl http://localhost:7000/file -r 2147483647-2147483747
```

**Additional context**
The error is due to the implementation using `InputStream#available()` to determine the max size, which returns an int and so can never represent files > 2GB.
Also note that according to the doc https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/11/docs/api/java.base/java/io/InputStream.html?is-external=true#available() available() does not need to return the actual size of the underlying stream. So is actually very likely to return values smaller than the actual size.
I would suggest  fixing this with a new method `Context#seekableStream(InputStream in, String contentType, long size)`

