problem_statement:
"AccessManager" in Javalin 6 is buggy, beforeMatched and before
**Actual behavior (the bug)**
As in the Migrationguide stated, the old AccessManager behaviour can be constructed via the `beforeMatched` method which states to be called even for static files. I have multiple `staticFiles` files enabled, also webjars. `beforeMatched` only gets called for webjars (which seem to be handled by an internal handler) and my manually defined handlers, but not for `/` and `/other`. If i change `beforeMatched` to `before` the behaviour is as expected, called for every request, but `ctx.routeRoles()` is empty, breaking the access manager.

Sample output from the "AccessManager" using `beforeMatched`:
```
2024-05-02 14:28:56,429 INFO  [JettyServerThreadPool-55] App: beforeMatched: [0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1] GET /admin/channels > [ADMIN]
2024-05-02 14:28:56,430 WARN  [JettyServerThreadPool-55] App: access forbidden: GET /admin/channels for [0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1] Chrome
(no /other!)
```
and with `before`:
```
2024-05-02 14:42:44,847 INFO  [JettyServerThreadPool-55] App: before: [0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1] GET /admin/channels > []
2024-05-02 14:42:47,716 INFO  [JettyServerThreadPool-31] App: before: [0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1] GET /other/test.html > []
(other but no roles)
```

**Expected behavior**
beforeMatched to be called for pretty much **EVERY** request.

**To Reproduce**
```java
config.staticFiles.enableWebjars();

config.staticFiles.add(staticFiles -> {
    staticFiles.hostedPath = "/";
    staticFiles.directory = "/public";
    staticFiles.location = Location.CLASSPATH;
});

config.staticFiles.add(staticFiles -> {
    staticFiles.hostedPath = "/other";
    staticFiles.directory = "./path/in/filesystem";
    staticFiles.location = Location.EXTERNAL;
});

// simplified
javalin.beforeMatched(ctx -> {
  LOG.info("beforeMatched: {} {} {} > {}", ctx.ip(), ctx.method(), ctx.path(), ctx.routeRoles());

  if (ctx.routeRoles().isEmpty()) {
      if (ctx.path().startsWith("/other/")) {
          // allow localhost only
          if ("127.0.0.1".equals(ctx.ip())) {
              return;
          }
          throw new ForbiddenResponse();
      }

      LOG.warn("handler {} {} has no access role defined!", ctx.method(), ctx.path());
      return;
  }

  if (ctx.routeRoles().contains(AccessRole.PUBLIC)) {
      return;
  }

  if (!ctx.routeRoles().contains(getLoggedOnRoles(...)) {
      LOG.warn("access forbidden: {} {} for {} {}", ctx.method(), ctx.path(), ctx.ip(), ctx.userAgent());
      ctx.skipRemainingHandlers().redirect("/admin/login");
  }
});
```

**Additional context**
Java 11 with Javalin version 6.1.3.

